%% Updated: 2026-06-26.
%% Purpose: Show who can view proposal list and review proposals, with creator vs owner/manager nuance.
%% Excludes: Proposal submit details, withdraw flow, scoring internals.
%% Related: act_02b_marketplace_apply.mmd — proposal submit; act_02e_marketplace_application_exceptions.mmd — exceptions.
%% Reader intent: Clarify who can view/review proposals without inferring a narrower rule than runtime actually enforces.
%% Key boundary: Focuses on permission chain only, not scoring or proposal lifecycle.
%% Current caveat: Current runtime allows creator plus project owner/manager paths; callers must pass project-role context correctly.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Requester as Requester
    participant Query as GetMarketplaceTaskApplicationsQuery
    participant PCmd as ProcessMarketplaceApplicationCommand
    participant Rules as TaskAssignmentRules
    participant PM as ProjectMember
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over Requester,DB: Scenario A: View proposal list

    Requester->>Query: GET /tasks/:taskId/applications
    Query->>Rules: canProcessApplication(actorId, creatorId, 'approve', isTaskAlreadyAssigned, isProjectOwnerOrManager)

    alt actor == task.creator_id
        Rules-->>Query: allow (creator)
    else actor is project_owner or project_manager
        Query->>PM: Check project_members where user_id + role IN (project_owner, project_manager)
        PM-->>Query: membership found
        Rules-->>Query: allow (owner/manager)
    else neither
        Rules-->>Query: deny
    end

    Note over Requester, DB: Scenario B: Review (approve/reject) proposal

    Requester->>PCmd: POST /applications/:id/process
    PCmd->>Rules: canProcessApplication(actorId, creatorId, action, isTaskAlreadyAssigned, isProjectOwnerOrManager)

    alt actor == task.creator_id
        Rules-->>PCmd: allow (creator)
    else actor is project_owner or project_manager
        PCmd->>PM: Lazy-load project_members for this task's project
        PM-->>PCmd: membership
        Rules-->>PCmd: allow (owner/manager)
    else neither
        Rules-->>PCmd: deny → 403
    end

    alt action == 'approve' AND task already assigned
        Rules-->>PCmd: deny → 'cannot approve more'
    end

    Note over Requester, DB: Key nuance
    Note over Requester, DB: Keep creator and project owner/manager paths aligned.
    Note over Requester, DB: canProcessApplication allows creator OR project owner/manager.
    Note over Requester, DB: Frontend proposal page still requires owner/manager capability.
    Note over Requester, DB: Do not claim project manager or org admin paths are excluded.
